# RPG Mock Service: Post-Mortem Logs & Architecture Decision Records (ADR)

This document serves as the repository's operational maintenance log. It contains formal engineering post-mortems for pipeline failures encountered during deployment, alongside production Architecture Decision Records (ADRs).

---

## 1. INCIDENT POST-MORTEM: AUTOMATED PIPELINE TIMEOUTS
* **Incident Date:** June 2026
* **Severity:** Medium (Blocked CI/CD Release Loop)
* **Status:** Resolved

### 1.1 Problem Description
The original continuous integration build script utilized traditional manual container commands to spin up, copy, and execute validation scripts inside an active container environment. The workflow relied on executing "docker cp test.js rpg-running:/usr/src/app/test.js" followed by "docker exec rpg-running node test.js". 

While this execution pattern succeeded on isolated local developer workstations, pushing this sequential pattern to individual headless GitHub Actions runners caused structural hangs. Because the cloud runner environment could not cleanly manage the lifecycle of the detached container thread asynchronously, the step locked up and hit the maximum pipeline runtime timeout limit.

### 1.2 Root Cause Analysis (RCA)
Headless virtualization platforms require synchronous exit signals to tear down virtual testing steps. The runner script did not programmatically hook into the underlying container execution PID, leaving the network socket open and blocking the build environment from shutting down.

### 1.3 Corrective Action / Resolution
The automated workflow definition (.github/workflows/ci.yml) was updated to decouple verification from interactive container execution. The application is now initialized directly within the runner instance as an isolated background worker via the "node app.js &" process flag. 

By capturing the process ID immediate fallback (SERVER_PID=$!), the engineering pipeline now triggers a native system signal (kill $SERVER_PID) the exact millisecond downstream testing scripts complete. This guarantees clean environment teardown and prevents build freezes.

